e/runner/work/deepseek-harness/deepseek-harness/dist/npm/deepseek-ai-dsh-native-command-0.1.0-rc.8.tgz","_from":"file:/home/runner/work/deepseek-harness/deepseek-harness/dist/npm/deepseek-ai-dsh-native-command-0.1.0-rc.8.tgz","_nodeVersion":"24.19.0","_npmVersion":"11.17.0","dist":{"integrity":"sha512-bRaT8LOb2xmWQ88oSzM4+Y3N4Yy4J0tf15/kQTP53PY1FnOA5hGYWoRglQgfxIcJCrw4fEdUPie8Fff0dCOwdQ==","shasum":"fd8e2380217bda23fff938d97e1de1a94eb32ed2","tarball":"https://registry.npmmirror.com/@deepseek-ai/dsh-native-command/-/dsh-native-command-0.1.0-rc.8.tgz","fileCount":9,"unpackedSize":9600,"signatures":[{"keyid":"SHA256:DhQ8wR5APBvFHLF/+Tc+AYvPOdTpcIDqOhxsBHRwC7U","sig":"MEUCIQDHSHt6+OFYgXJQgeCncIoZMXibglJM15pV9CoOgo7WCgIgYaCfGRZPjw50GkE/7gunUgqgv8gTP0wORmPckpGlDHc="}],"size":4645},"_npmUser":{"name":"imccyu","email":"imccyu@gmail.com"},"directories":{},"maintainers":[{"name":"imccyu","email":"imccyu@gmail.com"},{"name":"tianyicui-deepseek","email":"tianyi@deepseek.com"}],"_npmOperationalInternal":{"host":"s3://npm-registry-packages-npm-production","tmp":"tmp/dsh-native-command_0.1.0-rc.8_1787153475364_0.06800609922869527"},"_hasShrinkwrap":false,"_cnpmcore_publish_time":"2026-08-19T15:31:15.516Z","publish_time":1787153475516,"_source_registry_name":"default"}},"bugs":{"url":"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/issues"},"description":"Zero-dependency no-shell execFile runner for host-native OS integrations: utf8 stdio capture, abort propagation, Windows hide","homepage":"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness#readme","license":"BSD-3-Clause","maintainers":[{"name":"tianyicui-deepseek","email":"tianyi@deepseek.com"},{"name":"imccyu","email":"imccyu@gmail.com"}],"readme":"# dsh-native-command\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA **zero-dependency no-shell `execFile` runner** shared by host-native OS integrations: one `runNativeCommand(command, args, signal)` call spawns the executable directly (never a shell string), captures utf8 stdout/stderr, propagates the caller's abort into child termination, and hides the transient console window on Windows. Failures reject with the exit `code` and both captured streams attached, so callers classify (missing tool, cancelled, real failure) without re-running anything.\n\nIts two consumers are the host-side native integrations: the [`directory-picker-native`](../../host/directory-picker-native/README.md) backend's OS chooser commands and the gateway's open-with-default-application hand-off ([`dsh-host-apiproxy`](../../host/apiproxy/README.md) `host.openPath`). The `NativeCommandRunner` type is their injectable command boundary.\n\nIt is a **library, not a service or plugin**: no `ctx`, registers nothing, holds no state, emits no events.\n\n## Surface\n\n```ts\nimport { runNativeCommand, type NativeCommandRunner } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-native-command'\n```\n\n## Model Experience\n\nNone, as this is host-side subprocess plumbing; nothing here reaches a model request.\n\n#### KV Cache effect\n\nNone; this package neither assembles nor sends a provider request.\n\n## Known Limitations and Deferred Work\n\n- **No output bounding** — both streams buffer unbounded in memory; every current caller invokes small native tools whose output is a path or an error line. Adopt `dsh-retention` bounding before pointing this at commands with meaningful output volume.\n","readmeFilename":"README.zh.md","repository":{"url":"git+https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness.git","type":"git","directory":"packages/util/native-command"},"_source_registry_name":"default"}